| PHILBRICK 1964  --  OP-AMP APPLICATION EQUATIONS                                   |
| Typical Operational Amplifier Applications                                         |
| for Modelling, Measuring, Manipulating & Much Else          August 1964            |
+====================================================================================+
| NOTATION / VARIABLES                                                               |
|   e          output voltage                                                        |
|   ei, e1..e4 input voltages                                                        |
|   i          current           Q, dQ   charge                                      |
|   R, Rf, C   resistance, feedback R, capacitance                                   |
|   Z          impedance         p       Laplace operator (= s)                      |
|   alpha, n, k dimensionless ratios / scale factors                                 |
|   E, E0, VR  reference / excitation voltages                                       |
|   ib         input bias current                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| FUNDAMENTALS (ideal op-amp, 1964 analog-computing language)                        |
|   Av -> infinity     Zin -> infinity     Zout -> 0                                 |
|   Virtual ground at inverting input                                                |
|   Closed-loop transfer function set by the feedback network, not the amp itself    |
|   p = d/dt  (Laplace)                                                              |
+====================================================================================+
| CIRCUIT TYPE                         TRANSFER EQUATION                             |
+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| Precision variable voltage source    | e = -VR * (R2 / R1)                         |
| Bridge amp (active / ultralinear)    | e = - (1/2) * alpha * E0                    |
| Bridge amp (floating supply)         | e = (1+n) * alpha * E / 2                   |
| Bridge amp (one end grounded)        | e = (n/2)*(1/(1+n))*(1-alpha)*E             |
| Bridge amp (mid-point grounded)      | e = (n * alpha / 4) * E                     |
| Charge amplifier                     | e = - dQ / C                                |
| Precise wide-band squarer            | e = ei^2                                    |
| Adding / subtractor                  | e = (Rf/R) * (e1 + e2 - e3 - e4)            |
| Current-to-voltage transresistor     | e = i * R           (ib < 1e-11 A)          |
| Precision AC-DC converter            | e ~ |ei|                                    |
| Precision FW rectifier-filter        | e = n * |ei| / (1 + R C p)                  |
| Stable integrator                    | e = - (1/RC) * INT ei dt                    |
|                                      |   = - ei / (R C p)                          |
| Follower (electrometer)              | e = ei              (ib < 1e-12 A)          |
| Precision oscillator                 | omega = 1/RC                                |
|                                      | e = E0 * sin(omega t)                       |
| Stable low-noise differentiator      | e = - R C p * ei                            |
| Impedance scaler                     | Zout = ((1+k)/k) * Zin                      |
| Variable controlled current source   | i = (ei - e0) / R                           |
| Precise wide-range logarithm         | e  proportional to  log(ei)   (n decades)   |
| 3-term PID controller                | e = -(1/alpha)*[R1/R + 1/(sCp) + s R2 C]*ei |
| Follower with gain (electrometer)    | e = (1+R) * ei      (ib < 1e-11 A)          |
| Negative impedance                   | Zin = -R            (S.C. stable)           |
